    "values": [
      {
        "value": "threatened",
        "source": "glottolog-cldf-v5.3",
        "note": "Highland Ecuadorian Quichua (10851) = Vulnerable (80 percent certain, based on the evidence available) (Calderón [qud]: \"shifting\"; home, all ages.\r\nCañar Highland Quichua [qxr]: \"threatened\"; \"Strong use of Quichua away from the road.\"\r\nChimborazo [qug]: \"developing\"\r\nImbabura Quichua [qvi]: Vigorous. All ages.\r\nLoja [qvj]: \"moribund\"; Mainly older adults. Positive attitude.\r\nNorthern Pastaza Quichua [qvz]: \"threatened\"; Home, community, religion. All ages. Negative attitudes. Most also\r\nuse Spanish [spa]. Used as L2 by Achuar-Shiwiar [acu], Waorani [auc].\r\nSalasca [qxl]: Home, community, agriculture. All ages. Positive attitude.\r\nNapo Quichua [qvo]: \"developing\".\r\n(Cotopaxi Quichua is not included as an entry in Ethnologue)) [Lewis et al. 2017](cldf:lewis:simons:etal:ed:17)",
        "scale": "glottolog-cldf-v5.3"
      },
      {
        "value": "Vulnerable",
        "source": "linguameta-452a21ad3dae",
        "scale": "linguameta-452a21ad3dae"
      }
