        "value": "Binary politeness distinction",
        "source": "wals-v2020.5",
        "note": "<div class=\"Example\"><table class=\"example\"><tr><td><p><i>kikin</i></p></td><td><p>2nd sg. hon.</p></td><td><p>- this form is derived from Proto-Quechua <i>kiki</i>- which</p><p>is used in non-northern Quechua as emphatic reflexive</p><p>pronoun, this useage is lost in Imbabura Quechua;</p><p>- usually, the honorific pronoun is accompanied with a</p><p>honorific suffix <i>-pa</i> in the verb;</p><p>- usage is like Spanish <i>usted</i>; used to addressteachers,</p><p>parents, superiors</p></td></tr></table></div>",
